<%# Layout for the communicator care plan PDF (Communicators::GenerateCarePlan).

    A separate layout+template pair rather than a branch inside
    layouts/pdf_printable.html.erb — the same rule that keeps pdf_marketing and
    pdf_printable apart. Two reasons here, and the second is load-bearing:

    1. render_wrappers_spec.rb asserts against pdf_printable's rendered HTML, so
       editing it to serve a second document changes bytes that spec reads.
    2. pdf_printable is architecturally a FIXED-PAGE layout — `@page { margin: 0 }`
       plus `.sheet { height: 11in; overflow: hidden }`. A care plan is however
       many pages the parent's answers come to. Rendered through that layout it
       would be silently clipped at 11 inches with the rest discarded.

    The brand tokens below are deliberately DUPLICATED from pdf_printable rather
    than extracted into a shared partial: extracting would change the byte
    content of that layout's <style> block, which is the thing its spec reads.
    If you edit a token here, edit it there.

    Two rails carry over unchanged from pdf_printable:

    1. Nothing is fetched over the network at render time. Nunito is inlined by
       Boards::Printables::Fonts; anything fetched mid-render fails silently
       into a fallback and nobody notices until it ships. (The avatar is a
       data: URI resolved BEFORE the render, so it doesn't break this.)
    2. Every colour is print-exact — print-color-adjust on html and body.

    NOTE ON @page: there is deliberately no `margin` here. Grover supplies the
    page margin, because Chrome renders the header/footer in a SEPARATE document
    that is clipped to nothing unless the page reserves margin for it. Adding
    `@page { margin: 0 }` — the obvious thing to copy from pdf_printable — makes
    the page numbers vanish with no error. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Care plan</title>

    <style>
      <%= Boards::Printables::Fonts.face_css %>

      :root {
        --navy: #13496f;
        --blue-mid: #0163aa;
        --cyan: #4ECDE6;
        --magenta: #C857E8;
        --cream: #FBF7F1;
        --ink: #1A1A1A;

        --cream-deep: #F3EADC;
        --cyan-tint: #E4F7FB;
        --magenta-tint: #F8EAFD;
        --brand-gradient: linear-gradient(135deg, #4ECDE6 0%, #0163AA 55%, #C857E8 100%);

        --rule: #E2E1DD;
        --muted: #5A5A5A;
        --alert: #B3261E;
        --alert-tint: #FDECEA;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

      html, body {
        -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
        print-color-adjust: exact;
      }

      /* White, not cream: this runs to three sheets on a school printer and a
         full-bleed tint on every one of them is a lot of toner for no gain.
         The cream is kept for the banded surfaces that earn it. */
      body {
        font-family: Nunito, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: #fff;
        font-size: 10.5pt;
        line-height: 1.45;
      }

      @page { size: letter; }

      /* ---- Page-break behaviour ----

         Deliberately NOT `break-inside: avoid` on .care-section as a whole. A
         built-in section can carry four fields plus eight detail lines of up to
         200 characters, which comfortably exceeds a page — and an unbreakable
         box taller than a page makes Chrome push the whole thing to the next
         sheet and leave a dead half-page behind it.

         Instead: keep the heading welded to its first row (.section-keep), and
         let everything after that flow. break-after: avoid on a heading alone
         has never been reliable in Chrome's print path; a wrapper with
         break-inside: avoid is. The wrapper is the mechanism, the break-after
         is only a hint. */
      .section-keep { break-inside: avoid; }
      .section-keep h2 { break-after: avoid; }
      .row, .item, .contact { break-inside: avoid; }
      p { orphans: 3; widows: 3; }

      /* ---- Masthead ---- */
      .masthead {
        background: var(--brand-gradient);
        color: #fff;
        padding: 14pt 18pt;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        border-radius: 10pt;
      }
      .masthead .eyebrow {
        font-size: 8pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        opacity: 0.92;
      }
      .masthead h1 { font-size: 19pt; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.15; }
      .masthead img.logo { height: 30pt; width: auto; display: block; }

      /* ---- Identity ---- */
      .identity {
        display: flex;
        gap: 14pt;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 14pt 0 12pt;
        border-bottom: 1.5pt solid var(--rule);
      }
      .identity .avatar {
        width: 74pt; height: 74pt;
        border-radius: 999pt;
        object-fit: cover;
        border: 2.5pt solid var(--cyan);
        background: var(--cyan-tint);
        flex: none;
      }
      .identity .avatar-placeholder {
        width: 74pt; height: 74pt;
        border-radius: 999pt;
        background: var(--cyan-tint);
        border: 2.5pt solid var(--cyan);
        flex: none;
      }
      .identity .who { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
      .identity h2 { font-size: 17pt; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.15; }
      .identity .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 9.5pt; margin-top: 2pt; }
      .identity .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 8.5pt; margin-top: 5pt; }

      .qr { text-align: center; flex: none; width: 96pt; }
      .qr img { width: 76pt; height: 76pt; display: block; margin: 0 auto; }
      /* The URL is printed as text under the QR on purpose: these get
         photocopied and handed to people who don't have a phone camera out. */
      .qr .url {
        font-size: 6.5pt;
        color: var(--muted);
        word-break: break-all;
        line-height: 1.25;
        margin-top: 3pt;
      }

      /* ---- Emergency block ---- */
      .emergency {
        border: 2pt solid var(--alert);
        border-radius: 8pt;
        padding: 11pt 13pt 12pt;
        margin-top: 14pt;
        background: var(--alert-tint);
      }
      .emergency h2 {
        font-size: 12.5pt;
        font-weight: 900;
        color: var(--alert);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        margin-bottom: 7pt;
      }
      .emergency .row { margin-bottom: 5pt; }
      .emergency .row:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

      .contacts { margin-top: 9pt; }
      .contacts h3 {
        font-size: 9pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        color: var(--alert);
        margin-bottom: 5pt;
      }
      .contact {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 10pt;
        padding: 4pt 0;
        border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(179, 38, 30, 0.25);
      }
      .contact .name { font-weight: 800; }
      .contact .rel { color: var(--muted); font-size: 9pt; }
      .contact .phone { font-weight: 800; white-space: nowrap; }

      /* ---- Care sections ---- */
      /* Sits inside the first section's .section-keep, not above the loop, so
         it can't strand at the foot of a page with the first section overleaf.
         The margin collapses against the section's own top margin, hence the
         .first override below. */
      .care-heading {
        font-size: 12.5pt;
        font-weight: 900;
        color: var(--navy);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        margin-bottom: 6pt;
      }

      .care-section { margin-top: 12pt; }
      .care-section.first { margin-top: 18pt; }
      .care-section h2 {
        font-size: 12pt;
        font-weight: 900;
        color: var(--navy);
        padding-bottom: 3pt;
        border-bottom: 1.5pt solid var(--cyan);
        margin-bottom: 6pt;
      }

      .row { margin-bottom: 5pt; }
      .row .label {
        font-size: 8.5pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.07em;
        color: var(--muted);
      }
      .row .value { font-size: 10.5pt; }

      .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4pt; margin-top: 2pt; }
      .chip {
        background: var(--cyan-tint);
        border: 0.75pt solid var(--cyan);
        border-radius: 999pt;
        padding: 1.5pt 7pt;
        font-size: 9.5pt;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .items { margin-top: 6pt; }
      .item {
        padding: 3pt 0;
        border-top: 0.75pt solid var(--rule);
        font-size: 10pt;
      }
      .item .k { font-weight: 800; }

      .muted { color: var(--muted); }

      .footnote {
        margin-top: 20pt;
        padding-top: 8pt;
        border-top: 0.75pt solid var(--rule);
        font-size: 8pt;
        color: var(--muted);
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
